rows = {}
rows[88] = ("**The field-level frame for type-(B) fields: over ℚ(√59), ℚ(√83), ℚ(√131) either every four-colouring of the plane is periodic or some one is not (`F(R) ∈ {0, P(R)}`), every periodic one is local at the dyadic place (`P(R) = R ∩ 𝔓⁴`), so the whole four-colour rigidity question is whether the single pair `(0, 4)` is forced** (FS-86; the theorems `plans/FS86-derivation.md` FS86-A1, A2, V1–V4, V3ram, B1-LR, LP, B1-LD, B1-D8, CL2). "
"**[hand, two derivations (Poros (plan), the plan's §0.3; verifier B1 blind); V3 given FS-66's certificates at 11 (and 19 for 83, 131) and `[Zhang2012]` Thm 1.8(i)]** "
"`R = ℤ[U_F]` is the ring of elements integral at every stable prime (Lemma R, for real `F` with `F(i)/ℚ` Galois and no stable prime ramified in `F(i)/F`: B1 stated it wider, and it fails at a ramified dyadic place, CL2); `F(R)` is an ideal and every non-zero ideal has finite index (V2); a periodic colouring factors through the categorical product of the stable local towers, every odd factor of all-levels independence ratio `< 1/4` — at 11 and 19 only by FS-66's certificates (Hoffman's 0.2855 and 0.2756 fail), the thinnest margin at 31 (`1/4 − 2.745·10⁻⁶`), the ramified place by **Lemma P, new here: the primitive-character bound `|λ| ≤ 2p^{m−1}`, and with it FS-66's certificates, carried to ramified towers** — so Zhang's MIS-normality pulls every colour class back from the dyadic tower (V3), and `𝔓⁴ = (4)` gives V4. The dyadic local plane of every `d ≡ 3 (mod 8)` is row 67's (A1). So the stub's \"yes, `P₄ ≠ 0`\" was free, and the milestone's question is `F(R)`. "
"**Not claimed:** `F(R)` for any type-(B) field (FS-86's question, open); V3 without FS-66's certificate at 11 (a gap exactly there); the frame's transfer to ℚ(√2,√3) (argued, row 93); anything at ℚ(√11) beyond B1-D8 (`F = P = 0` by row 66's gap transport, not MIS-normality: the plan's §0.4 side claim was false). **Prior art:** the dichotomy and the field-level `P` not found; Zhang's product step, of which `[GodsilEtAl2020]` Cor. 4.4 is the vector-colouring form.",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` §1, `plans/FS86-B1-verification.md`, `plans/FS86-dyadic-rigidity.md` §0, `plans/POROS-2026-09-25-fs86-plan.md` §3, `data/fs86/{stageA,b1}/`")
rows[89] = ("**Every four-colouring of the plane over K = ℚ(√3, √11) is, on each `R_K`-coset, a pullback from row 67's `P₄` at one of K's two dyadic places, and `F(R_K) = P(R_K) = 4R_K`** (FS-86; FS86-VK). "
"**[hand + cert + external, two derivations (the planner, completed by Poros (plan)'s equal-ratio step; B1 blind); given one non-zero forced difference — row 78's certificate or row 85's derivation (given Parts's trees); FS-66's certificate at 11 carried to K's ramified 11-towers by Lemma P; `[Zhang2012]`]** "
"The two dyadic factors have equal ratio 1/4 (Zhang's case (ii)), so the place is chosen by tightness: `P_m × P′_m` is four-tight with least eigenspace the pure characters, so each colour class is `a(x) + b(y)` and lies at one place. **Positive control by formula:** `[Fischer1994]`'s ℤ/4 colouring reads exactly one dyadic prime, at level 3; `8/3, 8/9, 16/3` and row 78's `v` lie in `4R_K` (`1/3 ∈ R_K`), `2P` does not (the wall stands). On de Grey's lattice `4R_K ∩ Λ = 4Λ ⊋ 8Λ = F(Λ)` (row 85): the field forces more than the lattice — the Moser ring's `8R`-periodic colourings (Speyer, Hubai, 2018) do not extend, since `ζ₁₂` and `i` force period 4. The window form without VK (C14-K = VC-C7) is in row 92. "
"**Not claimed:** that different cosets choose the same place (they need not); the extension form along a fixed embedding (false, FS86-W-A1K); anything above four colours. **Prior art:** Speyer (Polymath16, 25 April and 3 May 2018; `[Speyer2018]`) posed the level-one question on the Moser ring; the field-level classification not found in the threads, the wiki's *Algebraic formulation* page (no ring with `i` or `ζ₁₂`) or `[Fischer1994]`; zbMATH and the Johnson papers not searched.",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` FS86-VK, `plans/FS86-B1-verification.md` VK, C2 (D6, D7), C3, `plans/FS86-dyadic-rigidity.md` §0.4, `data/fs86/b1/fischer_vk_control.gp`")
rows[90] = ("**The plane over `ℚ₂(√3)` is four-colour rigid — every four-colouring of it, measurable or not, is a pullback from `P₄` on each coset of `O`, forced group exactly `𝔓⁴` — so the planes over ℚ(√59) and every real field inside `ℚ₂(√3)` are dense subgraphs of one rigid local plane, and four-colour rigidity over them is an extension (realisability) question** (FS-86; FS86-dB-E, W1, dB-A, dB-A1, W-A1K, dB-B, dB-Atf, dB-T1). "
"**[hand + certificate (row 78), or given Parts's trees (row 85); plus FS38-D2-B — two derivations (de Bruijn; verifier W blind, needing only `ℤ[T] = O`, row 78's forced `v` with `v_𝔓(v) = 6`, D2-B at level 6 and `P₄`'s pairwise freedom); the grade corrected from \"given VK\"]** "
"**Extension form** (A1): for 59, 83, 131, `F(R) ≠ 0` iff every four-colouring of the field plane extends to the local plane, per coset; (⇐) for every real `F ⊂ ℚ₂(√3)`; at K only along one of its two embeddings, chosen per coset. 2-adically locally constant colourings are pullbacks (B). **Where triangles enter:** only in Theorem A's input — every known local forcer is built on `√3` — so the sharp local question is whether `4 ∈ F_tf`, the differences forced in the local plane by triangle-free finite configurations (the 2-adic forced-pair form of Soifer 55.1), and `4 ∈ F_tf` iff some number field inside `ℚ₂(√3)` carries a finite triangle-free forcer of `(0, 4)` (T1; two derivations; the smooth case suffices, `[Kuhlmann2016]` Cor. 5.10 covering the singular case). The killing test passed on K1 with this result, under the pre-announced standard that a necessary condition shown to hold counts. "
"**Not claimed:** that the local rigidity separates fields — it holds identically at ℚ(√11) (`F = 0`) and K (`F ≠ 0`); `4 ∈ F_tf` or its negation; `F(R)` for any type-(B) field. **Prior art:** the chromatic number of `p`-adic planes (`[Madore2015]` ¶1.5, `[BardestaniMallahiKarai2017]`); a rigidity statement for a local plane not found; a full gate on it is owed.",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` §3, `plans/FS86-C-deBruijn.md` §1, §5.1, `plans/FS86-V-W-verification.md` W-A–W-B, `plans/FS86-V-D-verification.md` VD-T1, `plans/POROS-2026-09-25-fs86-competition.md` §7, `data/fs86/v-w/`")
rows[91] = ("**Every natural construction of a non-periodic four-colouring of a type-(B) plane is impossible — two-pullback patchworks, one pullback with any residue alternative, defects confined to a half-space, threshold walls, stripes, 2-adically continuous colourings, Kempe swaps, gapped targets of any extension, character colourings of finite type — and HD1 (no non-torsion band character) is equivalent to one finite exact certificate** (FS-86; FS86-dB-D, dB-Dp, dB-H, dB-D0, dB-W, dB-B, dB-HD4, Cx-C7, dB-Theta, dB-HDfin, dB-Sv, dB-HDint, dB-HDcert, VD-1, VX-C, VX-Cp, VX-11, Cx-C15, dB-C0, dB-S, dB-K3, Cx-C11). "
"**[hand; two derivations where marked, each with a blind verifier]** **D** (agreeing everywhere with one of two pullbacks ⟹ periodic, every field with row 67's tower, K and non-real included; a pullback for real `F` with no V3) and **D′** (one pullback plus any residue-determined alternative ⟹ a pullback, every real `F` with row 67's tower, no V3 — X's Lemma C′ widening): de Bruijn, verifier X. **H** (every number field, any number of colours: a colouring agreeing with a gap-free periodic one on an additive half-space equals it — a non-periodic four-colouring disagrees with every pullback in every archimedean direction): de Bruijn, X. **D₀** (no threshold walls, `h ≠ 0`; false at `h = 0`): de Bruijn, W. **HD4** (Kempe swaps of pullbacks are pullbacks: the voltage-escape screen is blind at the field level): de Bruijn, X. **HD1-fin = C10** (every finite-type band character in S2 is a pullback character): de Bruijn and Coxeter independently, C as a corollary of row 92. **HD1-cert** (HD1 iff some finitely generated `Λ₁ ∋ 1` has `θ(1) ∈ {1/4, 1/2, 3/4}` on `Θ₄(Λ₁)`; semi-decidable, no size bound; a non-torsion point gives `F(R) = 0`): de Bruijn, D. **C0** (unit-distance pair correlations on any real field admit a purely archimedean spectrum; W's repaired measure meets every two-point constraint with 95 % of its mass non-periodic): de Bruijn, Poros (competition), W. One mind each: stripes, C15, Prop. S, (S-v), K3, C11. **Together:** a \"no\" must disagree with every pullback in every archimedean direction, be no patchwork of these kinds and no phase pattern, be 2-adically discontinuous, and any band character of it must read infinitely many split places. "
"**Not claimed:** `F(R)` for any type-(B) field; evidence for rigidity (no-gos bound constructions, not the answer; G21); HD1; the three-phase case. D₀, D′ and H hold at ℚ(√11), where `F = 0`, so none separates it from ℚ(√59) alone — V3 does. **Prior art:** the annihilator method (`[KariSzabados2016]`, `[HervaKari2023]`) converts an identity into line-periodic sums and supplies none; nothing stating D or H found (a light gate).",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` §4–§7, `plans/FS86-C-deBruijn.md` §2, §4.1, §6, §7, `plans/FS86-C-Coxeter.md` round 2 steps 1–2, 6, `plans/FS86-V-X-verification.md`, `plans/FS86-V-W-verification.md` W-C0, W-D₀, `plans/FS86-V-D-verification.md` VD-cert, `data/fs86/{comp-debruijn,comp-coxeter,v-x,v-w,v-d}/`")
rows[92] = ("**Measurable windows cannot colour type-(B) planes non-periodically: over every field in S2, a four-colouring read off finitely many local coordinates through measurable windows is one pullback at the tight place, hence periodic — so FS-64's adelic window colouring and FS-83's layer method at four colours, with any finite set of places, cannot give `F(R) = 0`; and over ℚ(√47) and ℚ(√167) no measurable window four-colouring exists at all** (FS-86; FS86-Cx-C14, VC-C2, VC-C3, Cx-C14p, Cx-C14K, CL1). "
"**[hand, two derivations (Coxeter's third seat; verifier C blind, the same route, sharpened to one coset); at every real place it rests on `[AmbrusEtAl2023]` Thm 1, `m₁(ℝ²) ≤ 0.2470` — external, computer-assisted, published, not re-checked here (its audit a named post-close item; this grade to be upgraded in place); also V3's all-levels bounds and row 67]** "
"A measurable window form of Zhang's No-Homomorphism lemma and product rule; the local ratios: real places `m₁`, odd stable places their all-levels ratios, split places → 0; the non-tight part strictly below 1/4 (Hoffman's 0.2871 for the plane would not suffice); one good fibre, then the tight plane's gap-freeness gives the pullback at every point. Sharp: fails at ℚ(√11) (`Γ₇`'s 2/7; C9, row 94) and at K (a second tight place: every window colouring local at one tight place, C14-K = VC-C7, by product tightness, no VK). Triangle-blind (holds at ℚ(√2,√3), row 93). C14′: windows proper off a null set give periodic colourings for almost every placement. **Type (A), the close's corollary (one mind):** every factor has ratio `< 1/4`, so no measurable proper four-colouring of the product exists, for sets of places whose split places are odd (C14.2 at `p = 2`, where their dyadic places split, not checked). "
"**Not claimed:** non-measurable colourings or infinitely many places — the whole remaining question, HD1's infinite-type gap; anything at five colours (the count fails at the real place: Croft's `m₁ ≥ 0.22936 > 1/5`), so FS-59's and FS-64's five-colour questions at ℚ(√167) are untouched; complex places (a sketch). **Prior art:** `[Zhang2012]` (finite graphs); a measurable form not found.",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` §9, `plans/FS86-C-Coxeter.md` round 2 step 5, `plans/FS86-V-C-verification.md`, `data/fs86/comp-coxeter/c14/`")
rows[93] = ("**What propagates up a dyadic tower and what does not: every unramified quadratic dyadic tower containing `√3` is four-tight at every level; tightness does not propagate up constant-fibre towers in general; ℚ(√2,√3) is in S2 with triangles, and there the rigidity question is whether `√3` is a four-colour virtual edge** (FS-86; FS86-B1-LD, Cx-C12p1, B2-T0–T3, B3-T1, A3, A4, Cx-C12, Cx-C13p0, Cx-C13). "
"**[hand + tools exact]** **Corrected on the record:** FS38-L1's tightness half does not follow (colourability with Hoffman's bound gives `λ_min ≤ −d/(k−1)`, the same direction as the pull-back bound; B2, the owner); its slack half stands, and the 2-adic tower's tightness at every level rests on FS38-L2's non-strict half (Lemma D, B1) and the exact table — so row 67's propagation clause and G54's sentence were false as general statements. **The counterexample** (B2): `Λ₅₁₀`'s quotients `Q_m` (constant fibres from level 11) are tight at 1–5 and 11–14, slack at 6–10 and every `m ≥ 24`; yet every four-colouring of `Q_m`, `5 ≤ m ≤ 14`, is a pullback from `P₄` through the tight `Q₁₄` (G54's middle case again), and the infinite lattice is not tight. **The correct statement** (C12.1 = VC-C4; Coxeter, C blind): for `E/ℚ₂` with `√3 ∈ E` and residue field `𝔽₂` the tower is four-tight at every level unconditionally, and every colouring at level `m ≥ c` is a pullback from `P_c`. **ℚ(√2,√3)** (C12; Coxeter exact at levels 1–8, de Bruijn at 1–5, independently): its dyadic tower gives pullbacks from `P₄`, its odd stable places are the `p ≡ 23 (mod 24)`, so it is an S2 member with triangles; `√−3` is a unit vector mod `𝔓⁴` there (C13.0: iff `m ≤ e(E/ℚ₂)`), so `F(R) ≠ 0` iff `(0, 2)` is forced, and a yes makes every `√3`-pair a four-colour virtual edge (C13). `Λ₅₁₀` is rich (R1–R4; R4 a theorem below 29, measured at 29). "
"**Not claimed:** the frame's transfer to ℚ(√2,√3) re-derived (argued: Lemma R, Zhang); `F(R)` there; `Λ₅₁₀`'s `P` above level 14. **Prior art:** T721 (`[Soifer2024]` ch. 54: a triangle-full four-colour forced pair at distance 2 in ℚ(√2,√3)², consistent with C13).",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` §2, §8, `plans/FS86-B2-profile.md`, `plans/FS86-C-Coxeter.md` round 2 steps 3–4, `plans/FS86-V-C-verification.md` VC-12.1, VC-13.0, `data/fs86/{b2,b3,comp-coxeter/cs2}/`")
rows[94] = ("**Two neighbours of the class, decided: an explicit non-periodic four-colouring of ℚ(√11)'s plane by formula, and averaged rigidity for imaginary quadratic fields inside `ℚ₂(√3)` on the spectral class `T + A + Fin`, with a two-colourable quartic refuting its broader first statement** (FS-86; FS86-Cx-C9, dB-C, VD-7, VD-10, VD-11). "
"**[hand; C9 checked mod 7 by the owner; Theorem C two derivations (de Bruijn, downgraded by its own third seat; verifier D blind under the corrected hypothesis H*); VD-7 hand + exact PARI]** "
"**C9:** `θ = (2x + 3y)/7`, read at ℚ(√11)'s stable prime above 7, puts the 8 points of the circle over `𝔽₇` in `[2/7, 5/7]`; with an archimedean linear term below `1/28`, `⌊4θ⌋` is a proper, non-periodic four-colouring of the plane — FS-83's mechanism firing where the class hypothesis fails. **Theorem C under H*:** for `E` with closure `ℚ₂(√3)`, `i ∉ E`, and every other stable place (dyadic included) of normalised least eigenvalue `> −1/3` at every level, every translation-invariant random four-colouring whose spectral measure lies on `T + A + Fin` is almost surely a pullback; H* holds for every imaginary quadratic `E ⊂ ℚ₂(√3)` avoiding `𝔽₃, 𝔽₇, 𝔽₁₁, 𝔽₁₉` (ℚ(√−709)). **Refuted** (D; PARI, checked by the owner): the clause \"more generally a number field with no real place\" — a totally complex quartic with a `ℚ₂(√3)` place and two `ℚ₂` places ramified in `E(i)` is two-colourable, and a random shift of its two-colouring is an invariant four-colouring that is no pullback. "
"**Not claimed:** Theorem C's unrestricted form or its corollaries (`F_μ = P` for ℚ(√−709); `χ(E²) ≥ 4` through the complex place), which need Lemma X, open outside `T + A + Fin`. **Prior art:** the unit argument and the layer method (`[Fischer1990]`, G74); an explicit non-periodic four-colouring of a field plane not seen in print.",
"`plans/FS86-derivation.md` §4 (C9), §5, `plans/FS86-C-Coxeter.md` round 2 step 1, `plans/FS86-C-deBruijn.md` §4.2, §7.4, `plans/FS86-V-D-verification.md` VD-C, `data/fs86/v-d/`")
